                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "232910422",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198191601935",
                            "num_reviews": 12,
                            "playtime_forever": 1381,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 1381,
                            "last_played": 1786808326
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I had so many fond memories of playing this game's Demo on repeat on my 3DS as a kid.\nRecently stumbled across it on Steam and I knew it was time to finally play it for real.\n\n\"Witch and Hero\" is quite a simple game on the surface, given the premise being that you can only control half of your crew, but you'd be surprised at the amount depth the game develops with its resource management and timing later on.\n\nThat said, the game's start is a bit weak, a few of the big mechanics are unlocked along the course of the Campaign which makes the combat a bit plain for the first few stages, though this might've been more noticeable because I played through the game twice for 100%.\nAnother downside is the Campaign's very inconsistent difficulty curve. You'll work through 3-4 stages like usual and then the next will completely overwhelm you, requiring you to go back and grind the last stage for a considerable amount of time for a good few upgrades, but the next few stages after that will be a breeze again.\nWith how short the game is, having these grind stops is very jarring, but once you're finally through it all and fully decked out, the game's combat is a treat.\n\nFeaturing 2 bonus modes after beating the game, this could be a fun little passtime to pull up every now and then. The game's very charming and with how cheap the game is (not to mention that it often goes on sale too), there's really no reason to not pick it up give it a try.",
